{"id": 48, "ts": 1779731869.9219515, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I appreciate the points raised about Candidates\u202fA and\u202fD, but the lack of any concrete evidence of operational reliability or stress\u2011resilience for them leaves serious gaps in the safety\u2011critical profile we need for long\u2011haul flights.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC is the only candidate with an explicit \u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d rating and a proven ability to \u201ccreate a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d directly satisfying the two non\u2011negotiable criteria of operational reliability and crew cooperation.\u202fWhile C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude are concerns, they are less fatal than the uncertainty surrounding A\u2019s and D\u2019s reliability, and they can be addressed through crew\u2011resource\u2011training.\u202fCandidate\u202fB, although conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, has a noted weak memory for numbers\u2014a potential attention\u2011to\u2011detail risk\u2014and we have no concrete evidence of his reliability on long\u2011haul missions.\u202fTherefore, based on the strongest available evidence, I now recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
